<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Bardiche</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. 3'
Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>This very broad and heavy axe links the pole axes to the pole cleavers as a sort of transitional step between the two forms, although its only obvious use is as a military arm. A Bardiche head ranged from about 2 feet to over 3 feet length, and it was attached to its haft with two rings or a single one in those examples where the blade is shorter and backed with a hammer head or spike. The Bardiche in all of its forms was very heavy and cumbersome - more so by far than a halberd - and was used principally in Eastern Europe.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the bardiche is a weapon skill of its own, one of the polearms (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): two-handed, it slashes, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is slow, as two-handed weapons are. It is taught by the barbarians from guild level 18, the fighters from guild level 18, the knights from guild level 26 and the paladins from guild level 26.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
